{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kxfe8crnEfihz89NZmoLac","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target \"start\" \"end\" units %lthr JSON format\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/need-help-with-hr-based-workouts-in-bpm/120685\"},{\"title\":\"Workout builder\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/839\"},{\"title\":\"HR target missing from Garmin Connect workout upload\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-missing-from-garmin-connect-workout-upload/5483\"},{\"title\":\"Threshold HR Run setting not reflecting in workout\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/threshold-hr-run-setting-not-reflecting-in-workout/15286\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521?page=9\"},{\"title\":\"forum.intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/using-heart-rate-zones/90516\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up the exact `workout_doc` JSON schema for HR targets with `start`/`end` and `%LTHR` units. The results are forum posts, not API documentation, so the field names are unconfirmed.\n\nRelated details that did come up:\n\n- **Range defaults:** The default range for power and pace is 2.5%. For HR it is 1.5%. The API can override this with an `hrRange` query parameter, and use 0.0 to disable range.\n- **workout_doc fields:** A developer noted adding fields to workout_doc, including public Integer lthr;, which suggests LTHR is carried in that structure.\n- **%LTHR vs. %max HR:** One user reported that when using 80-84% HR, it calculates the range using your max heart rate. The percentages shown in the settings however, are based on the threshold HR. The fix offered was to use 80-84% LTHR.\n- **Mismatched LTHR:** Another user reported that with LTHR at 167, \"100m:00s 85-90% LTHR\" was actually taking 90%-95%, i.e. 149-158 bpm. That report is unresolved in the thread.\n- **Garmin export quirk:** The developer added a workaround: if the high end of a custom HR range would be 80 or less with 100 subtracted and there are no high ends of 250 or more then the values are used as is, applied only to Garmin-manufactured files.\n- **Garmin HR targets:** Sending targets as a percentage of LTHR is intended so workouts can be shared between users, but if the sending or receiving app have different LTHR, it doesn't work as intended.\n\nFor the exact JSON field names and units, the official intervals.icu API documentation or a direct test export of a workout would be the next place to check.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"181d603b-b36b-4a9a-8a90-28ba22c22902","uuid":"54688c5d-378b-4458-b891-a691322e106f","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:47:10.077Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target \"start\" \"end\" units %lthr JSON format","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01HAvQjuQzN2NFCPzhXz4jvM","content":[{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389"},{"title":"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157"},{"title":"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356"},{"title":"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/need-help-with-hr-based-workouts-in-bpm/120685"},{"title":"Workout builder","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/839"},{"title":"HR target missing from Garmin Connect workout upload","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-missing-from-garmin-connect-workout-upload/5483"},{"title":"Threshold HR Run setting not reflecting in workout","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/threshold-hr-run-setting-not-reflecting-in-workout/15286"},{"title":"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521?page=9"},{"title":"forum.intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/using-heart-rate-zones/90516"}]},"The search didn't turn up the exact `workout_doc` JSON schema for HR targets with `start`/`end` and `%LTHR` units. The results are forum posts, not API documentation, so the field names are unconfirmed.\n\nRelated details that did come up:\n\n- **Range defaults:** The default range for power and pace is 2.5%. For HR it is 1.5%. The API can override this with an `hrRange` query parameter, and use 0.0 to disable range.\n- **workout_doc fields:** A developer noted adding fields to workout_doc, including public Integer lthr;, which suggests LTHR is carried in that structure.\n- **%LTHR vs. %max HR:** One user reported that when using 80-84% HR, it calculates the range using your max heart rate. The percentages shown in the settings however, are based on the threshold HR. The fix offered was to use 80-84% LTHR.\n- **Mismatched LTHR:** Another user reported that with LTHR at 167, \"100m:00s 85-90% LTHR\" was actually taking 90%-95%, i.e. 149-158 bpm. That report is unresolved in the thread.\n- **Garmin export quirk:** The developer added a workaround: if the high end of a custom HR range would be 80 or less with 100 subtracted and there are no high ends of 250 or more then the values are used as is, applied only to Garmin-manufactured files.\n- **Garmin HR targets:** Sending targets as a percentage of LTHR is intended so workouts can be shared between users, but if the sending or receiving app have different LTHR, it doesn't work as intended.\n\nFor the exact JSON field names and units, the official intervals.icu API documentation or a direct test export of a workout would be the next place to check."],"durationSeconds":7.060476666999999,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Kxfe8crnEfihz89NZmoLac","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
